description:
## Objective

Implement T05 only: a read-only Multica Issue Snapshot Adapter that converts authoritative issue data into the frozen, framework-neutral `prepare_handoff_request` input shape. Base the work on `yzt-56-finding-gate-selfcheck@e218e6cec0a5a0cb9032805d46d6ed1107bd1978` in a new isolated worktree and branch. Do not merge to `main`; final merge remains a Human action.

## Owner and dependency

- Owner: 02 Context Engineer, continuing the Human-approved routing on the parent.
- Exact baseline: `e218e6cec0a5a0cb9032805d46d6ed1107bd1978`, which contains accepted T01-T04 behavior including the current-role Finding Gate.
- Use the actual deployed `multica` CLI capability and JSON contract; do not guess an API that is not present.
- Do not modify, clean, or overwrite `D:\AI\multica-memory`, any existing YZT worktree, or the product repository.

## Contract boundary

The adapter is framework-specific, but its output must validate against the existing frozen framework-neutral request schema. In particular:

- the request envelope contains `task_ref`, `project`, `target`, `purpose`, `task_snapshot`, `caller`, and `options` as the frozen schema requires;
- `task_snapshot` does not gain Multica-only fields and does not duplicate envelope fields such as `task_ref` or `project_id`;
- `task_ref` is a stable opaque reference in the form `multica://issue/YZT-N`;
- the Adapter may translate Multica concepts, but Memory Core and Native API schemas must remain unaware of Multica runtime semantics;
- the Adapter must not interpret Memory Scope policy, select Canonical context, call `prepare_handoff`, or publish any result.

## Required snapshot mapping

Read the actual issue and deterministically map, when present and authorized:

- issue identifier to stable `task_ref`;
- mapped Memory registry `project_id` to `project.project_id`;
- issue title and description;
- explicitly structured requirements and acceptance criteria;
- parent issue identifier to `parent_task_ref`;
- explicitly selected relevant decisions;
- target role and caller role supplied through the adapter boundary;
- current assignee only when the frozen request contract has an explicit need for that information; do not add an assignee field to Core schemas.

Project mapping must fail closed. A Multica project UUID, missing project, or null project is not automatically a Memory registry `project_id`. Require an explicit deterministic mapping supplied by configuration/caller and return a bounded error when no stable mapping exists.

Requirements, acceptance criteria, and relevant decisions must have deterministic provenance. Use explicit headings/markers from authoritative issue content and/or caller-selected comment IDs. Do not infer decisions from arbitrary discussion. Ordinary progress comments, run logs, status sync, and unrelated chatter must be excluded by default and must not perturb the task fingerprint.

## Read-only and side-effect constraints

- No Canonical Memory, Checkpoint, registry, issue, comment, assignment, status, or filesystem-backed Memory write.
- No issue comments, mentions, assignment triggers, or new Multica runs from adapter execution.
- No LLM/model/network semantic interpretation.
- No Memory rebuild or evidence regeneration.
- No package discovery or latest `CONTEXT_HANDOFF` lookup; that publishing/discovery responsibility belongs to T06.
- No T06 publishing, T07 Shared Skill, T08 Agent Instructions, replay, rollout, or enablement work.

## Required tests

Use mocked/captured deployed CLI JSON and cover at minimum:

- stable `multica://issue/YZT-N` reference construction;
- title, description, parent, explicit requirements, acceptance criteria, and selected-decision mapping;
- explicit project mapping success;
- null/missing/unmapped project fails closed;
- malformed CLI JSON, missing fields, command failure, and permission failure;
- deterministic ordering and byte-stable repeated adapter output;
- ordinary comments excluded by default and not fingerprint-significant;
- only explicitly selected decision comments admitted, with exact provenance;
- output validation against the frozen `prepare_handoff_request` schema;
- proof that no Multica fields leak into Native API/Core schema shapes;
- proof of no Canonical writes, no LLM calls, no Memory rebuild, and no Multica write commands;
- deployed CLI compatibility behavior, including a bounded stop on an incompatible CLI contract.

Run the complete accepted 188-test T04B suite plus all focused T05 tests, `python tools/chandoff.py scan`, the frozen compatibility checks, and Gates A/B/C. Report exact commands and results.

## Done criteria

```yaml
done:
  deployed_cli_contract_checked: true
  stable_task_ref: true
  explicit_project_mapping: true
  request_schema_valid: true
  deterministic_snapshot: true
  arbitrary_comments_in_fingerprint: 0
  memory_scope_policy_in_adapter: 0
  canonical_writes: 0
  multica_writes: 0
  llm_calls: 0
  rebuilds: 0
```

## Stop and handoff

Stop and report the smallest concrete incompatibility if the deployed CLI cannot provide a stable authoritative issue snapshot, project mapping cannot be made explicit, the frozen request schema is incompatible, or implementation would require Memory policy/Core changes or Multica writes.

When Ready for Review, set this issue to `in_review` and mention 01 Engineering Lead on the parent issue using `[@01 Engineering Lead](mention://agent/24f04aba-7da9-4371-bf89-685d7505a411)`. Include branch/commit, changed files, deployed-CLI compatibility evidence, focused and full tests, gates/scans, deviations, residual risks, and the recommended next Execution Decision.
